items.clause:
Documented information required by the quality management system and by this International Standard shall be controlled to ensure:
a) it is available and suitable for use, where and when it is needed;
b) it is adequately protected (e.g. from loss of confidentiality, improper use, or loss of integrity).

For the control of documented information, the
organization shall address the following
activities, as applicable:
a) distribution, access, retrieval and use;
b) storage and preservation, including preservation
of legibility;
c) control of changes (e.g. version control);
d) retention and disposition.

